## SEVERITY / VERDICT (decided HERE)
*Blocker:* any change to who can sign in on UAT (a label-`uat` cell that differs; a cell that was off at the base and is open at the head; a cell open at the base and off at the head other than label `demo` on the old demo name); any lock weakened (a weakening plant green in every cell); any check CI runs that is red from the head (**the shell step at `validate.sh:10` is one**; lint, typecheck, build, `audit-dev`, `check-shards`, the infra tests, a unit, shard or API test red from the head); a rendered page or component that differs base to head with the notice off or unset beyond the masked `useId` values; compiled `uat` or `dev` parameters that are not byte-equal; a compiled setting other than `HPSM_DEMO_NOTICE` that differs; a word, element, setting, header or environment variable added; a path outside the lane with changed behaviour; a secret; a non-ASCII byte or a person's name in an added line or the message. *Major:* a removed row whose property UAT still needs has no holder at the head, or its holder stays green under the plant that breaks the property; a claim in the builder's STATUS or commit message that your numbers contradict (cell counts, row counts, the "no UAT twin" claim of `:97`); a judgement of the builder's FOR TUESDAY item that your instrument contradicts. *Minor:* a false comment (the stale comments of FACTS, four groups); a plant that only closes UAT stays green (plant Y4: no row for a uat-named site with other platform markers); a missing pin for a measured-safe shape (a locked choose route sets no cookie). *Note:* the statement of work's Demo question (NOT judged: the hold); SQL Server, hosted CI, CodeQL and the other seven e2e shards NOT RUN; NO PR (the hold); the author e-mail; `uat` on a name holding both `-uat-` and `demo` opens at base and head (pre-existing, B797); the template still compiles `environmentName=demo` and the infra tests still pin its cell (fail closed); the live setting `HPSM_DEMO_NOTICE=off` is inert; the Dependabot notice; the way-back scripts; the `use-recent-api-versions` linter warnings (same at the base); the subject is 102 characters (the squash subject is yours); UAT held, not touched. **GO** = steps 0-8 measured, nothing above Note; **GO WITH FINDINGS** = Minor/Note only; **NO GO** on any Blocker or Major.

